WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.530
On Shabbat, a young
child falls into the sea.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.530
Long ago, the rabbis of the
Talmud asked a hard question:

3
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.940
what should be done?

4
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.370
Their answer: spread a net
and pull the child out,

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.980
on Shabbat itself.

6
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.980
So why are Jews who break Shabbat
to save a life praised, not blamed?

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:24.240
In this mission, you'll find out why
Jews see every single human life as holy.

8
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.950
Then you'll explore how Jews differ today,

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.530
from organ donation to the end of life.

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: find out why saving a
life on Shabbat is praised, not blamed.
